---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTABlock from '../../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';

const inviteEmail = site.email;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Account Setup — Cloudflare & GitHub | Groundwork Dental"
  description="One-time setup: do it live on Zoom with us, or create Cloudflare and GitHub yourself and invite Groundwork as admin. You own the accounts either way."
  noindex={false}
>
  <section class="bg-surface-2">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-16">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow text-sage-dark mb-4">Client guide</p>
        <h1 class="section-heading mb-6">Account setup: Cloudflare &amp; GitHub</h1>
        <p class="font-serif text-xl text-mid-gray leading-relaxed">
          You own the accounts. We build in them. You can remove our access anytime.
          This is a <strong class="text-charcoal font-normal">one-time setup</strong> (~15 minutes). Pick whichever option is easier.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-sm text-mid-gray mt-6">
          Prefer markdown?
          <a href="/guides/account-setup.md" class="text-sage-dark hover:underline">Download / copy the .md</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose-article text-lg">

        <h2>Choose one</h2>
        <div class="not-prose grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mb-8">
          <div class="border border-neutral-200 bg-surface-2 rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-sage-dark mb-2">Option 1</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-charcoal mb-2">Live on Zoom</h3>
            <p class="font-serif text-mid-gray text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
              We drive on a shared screen. You verify email and set passwords.
            </p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-charcoal"><strong>Best if</strong> you want zero guesswork.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-neutral-200 bg-surface-2 rounded-lg p-5">
            <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-sage-dark mb-2">Option 2</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-charcoal mb-2">You set up, invite us</h3>
            <p class="font-serif text-mid-gray text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
              You create Cloudflare + GitHub, then invite us as admin.
            </p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-charcoal"><strong>Best if</strong> you’re fine clicking through signups.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>Same end result either way:</strong> accounts in your name, Groundwork added as admin so we can build and deploy.
          Reply with <strong>Option 1</strong> or <strong>Option 2</strong> on your project thread.
        </p>

        <h2>Why this matters</h2>
        <p>
          Your website runs on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> (hosting, DNS, SSL) and lives in a <strong>GitHub</strong> repository (the code). Both should be in <strong>your practice’s name</strong>, not ours.
        </p>
        <p>
          After launch, your only required ongoing cost is domain renewal (~$12–15/year). Hosting stays free.
        </p>

        <h2>What you’ll need (both options)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A practice email you control (e.g. <code>front@yourpractice.com</code>)</li>
          <li>About 15 minutes</li>
          <li>Your domain registrar login nearby — <strong>don’t change DNS yet</strong></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Option 1 — We do it live on Zoom</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Reply on your project thread and we’ll schedule a short Zoom.</li>
          <li>We create Cloudflare and GitHub using <strong>your</strong> email (shared screen).</li>
          <li>You click the verification emails and set passwords.</li>
          <li>We add ourselves as <strong>Administrator</strong> (Cloudflare) and <strong>Collaborator</strong> (GitHub).</li>
          <li>We connect the site and prepare DNS. At go-live we cut over carefully so email keeps working.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>You don’t need to figure out nameservers or API tokens.</p>

        <h2>Option 2 — You create the accounts and invite us</h2>

        <h3>A. Cloudflare</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Go to <a href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up</a></li>
          <li>Sign up with your <strong>practice email</strong></li>
          <li>Verify the email → set a strong password (save it)</li>
          <li>Use the <strong>Free</strong> plan</li>
          <li><strong>Manage Account</strong> → <strong>Members</strong> → <strong>Invite</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Email: <code>{inviteEmail}</code></li>
              <li>Role: <strong>Administrator</strong></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Send the invite</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>B. GitHub</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Go to <a href="https://github.com/signup" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/signup</a></li>
          <li>Use the <strong>same practice email</strong> when possible</li>
          <li>Verify email → set a password (Free plan is fine)</li>
          <li>When we send your repo link: <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Collaborators</strong> → <strong>Add people</strong></li>
          <li>Invite <code>{inviteEmail}</code> (or the GitHub username we send) — <strong>Write</strong> or <strong>Admin</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <h3>C. Tell us where the domain lives</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Where your domain is registered (GoDaddy, Google, Namecheap, Wix, Squarespace, etc.)</li>
          <li>Whether you can log in to that account</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>D. Do not change nameservers yet</h3>
        <p>
          Don’t update nameservers or delete DNS records until we say so. Office email depends on MX records. We’ll copy those safely before cutover.
        </p>

        <h2>What happens at launch</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Preview stays on a temporary URL until you’re ready</li>
          <li>Production hosting moves into <strong>your</strong> Cloudflare account</li>
          <li>We copy DNS (especially email / MX), then connect your real domain</li>
          <li>You get a handoff doc with every login</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Can developers still use APIs and AI tools?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Yes.</strong> If Groundwork is a Cloudflare Administrator and a GitHub collaborator, we create API tokens <em>inside your account</em> for our deploy tools. You can revoke them anytime. If you remove our access, the site keeps running.
        </p>

        <h2>Checklist — copy into your reply</h2>
        <pre class="font-mono text-sm bg-surface-2 border border-neutral-200 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap text-charcoal">Option chosen: 1 (Zoom) / 2 (I’ll invite you)

Cloudflare account created: Yes / Not yet / N/A (doing Zoom)
Practice email used: ________
Groundwork invited as Cloudflare Administrator: Yes / Not yet / N/A
GitHub account created: Yes / Not yet / N/A
Groundwork invited on GitHub: Yes / Not yet / N/A
Domain registrar (where the domain is): ________
I can log into the registrar: Yes / No / Not sure</pre>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${inviteEmail}`}>{inviteEmail}</a> — or reply on your project thread.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Don’t change DNS or nameservers until we confirm email records are copied.</strong> That’s the one step that can break mail if done early.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABlock
    heading="Ready when you are"
    subheading="Reply with Option 1 (Zoom) or Option 2 (you’ll invite us). Same result either way — about 15 minutes, one time."
    primaryCTA="Get Started"
    primaryHref="/get-started"
    secondaryCTA="How It Works"
    secondaryHref="/how-it-works"
  />
</BaseLayout>
